%\" (strings)\nempty_pipe_detection: \"on\" / \"on\"\n\nAccuracy class axis config:\n- mpe lower: Class 1 → 3 %; Class 2 → 5 %\n- mpe upper: Class 1 → 1 %; Class 2 → 2 %\n- mpe upper in service: Class 1 → 2 %; Class 2 → 3 %\n\nHmm — one concern: including \"in_service\" attribute is interpretive. Let me name it \"maximum_permissible_error_upper_flowrate_zone_second_row\"? That's awkward but neutral. I'll compromise: name \"maximum_permissible_error_upper_flowrate_zone_in_service\". Go.\n\nType-level characteristics final list:\n- q2_over_q1: 1.6\n- q4_over_q3: 1.25\n- measuring_principle: \"Electromagnetic water meter\"\n- accuracy_class: [\"1\",\"2\"]? value must be single — use recommendation.accuracy_classes [1,2] and skip here. Or value \"1 and 2\". I'll skip type_level (covered by recommendation + model_level).\n- water_pressure_class: \"MAP16\"\n- maximum_admissible_pressure: 1.6 MPa\n- pressure_loss_class: \"ΔP 40\"\n- environmental_class: \"O\"\n- operating_temperature_range: {-25,55} °C\n- electromagnetic_environment_class: \"E1, E2\"\n- mechanical_class: \"B, O\"\n- connection_type: \"Flanged\"\n- minimum_straight_length_inlet_pipe: 0 mm\n- minimum_straight_length_outlet_pipe: 0 mm\n- flow_profile_sensitivity_class: \"U0 D0\"\n- flow_conditioner: \"No\"\n- installation_orientation: \"any\"\n- reverse_flow: \"designed to measure\"\n- eut_test_category: \"Electromagnetic water meter\"\n- eut_test_case: \"D\"\n- volume_display_resolution: skip (model_level).\n- temperature_class: string summary \"PTFE: T90/T50/T30; Rilsan: T50/T30 (from DN50); Ebonite: T50/T30 (from DN200); Polypropylene: T50/T30\" — the liner matrix table covers this; skip to reduce noise. Actually keep a small one? Skip.\n\nNow issuing_authority:\nname: \"Czech Metrology Institute\", address_lines: [\"Okružní 31\", \"638 00 Brno\", \"Czech Republic\"], person_responsible: \"Jan Kalandra\".\n\nApplicant: ISOIL INDUSTRIA SPA — address_lines [\"Via F.lli Gracchi, 27\", \"Cinisello Balsamo\", \